{"kind":"request","text":"Checker: amend the re-issued URL Stage 2 due-query contract to fit the unchanged query runtime.","body":{"conditions":"The public query authorizer permits only avg/coalesce/count/ifnull/max/min/sum/total. SQLite LIKE/GLOB and substr/instr are denied, so host-suffix and url-prefix exclusions cannot be applied by the shipped query. A bounded keyed fold also cannot retroactively mark all prior observations when exclusions change. Preferred no-runtime amendment: let the due query select observations lacking a fresh provider verdict; query enabled exclusions separately; make the Stage 3 companion the mandatory exact/suffix/prefix/built-in filter immediately before egress. Retain the four tables, single fold, prefix host check, deterministic day_utc, and no new egress. Alternative: authorize a query/runtime profile change and RuntimeID bump. Please ratify one path and correct or replace db73307c; shipping its current due query would falsely claim exclusion enforcement.","to":"d50369731a941ee752b3a07cd33b8c7e9b4dbf1ead69532463a3df851bf2bd2f"}}